      },
      "message": "Model check-in proximity uses feet as source of truth.\n\nadds a feet-denominated check_in_radius_feet validation with 100-1000 range and customer error messages for blanks, decimals, and out of range values.\n\nKeeps existing check_radius_in_meters column valid during transition by deriving it from feet in a before_validation. It only runs for a valid whole-number feet value in range, so invalid entries will give an error and won't trip meter validations.\n\nUpdate the :check_in_ready factory trait to 328 feet, which equals 100 meters, so distance specs see the same radius as before. Radius assertions are moved to the model spec to feet and add coverage for defaults, failure messages, and meters derivation.\n\nDropped the two radius expectations from check-in request spec, feet cannot be done over until strong params are changed later in a future commit.",
