  {
    "sha": "87cb60710296b1f10cec75979a1cdc5afacb211f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOUOlySdoAKDg3Y2I2MDcxMDI5NmIxZjEwY2VjNzU5NzlhMWNkYzVhZmFjYjIxMWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "fernandomunozgarza",
        "email": "fer.munoz2012@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-22T07:35:01Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "fernandomunozgarza",
        "email": "fer.munoz2012@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-22T07:35:01Z"
      },
      "message": "Drops meters radius column so feet is used.\n\nRemove check_in_radius_meters and its positive-radius constraint. The model no longer validates meters or derives it from feet, so feet is only left. Only the migration references feet since it was introduced.\n\nDown migration is reversible but will not be precise. It re-adds meters column and backfills it with feet values, rounded/floored, and satisfies the positive constraint. It cannot restore the exact pre-drop meters value.\n\nSpecs for meters derivation and the second-meters error case are removed. Invalid feet still produces a clear error, blank, whole-number, and range examples are also tested.",
      "tree": {
